namespace BoatsNBeasts.Core;

internal static partial class DeepRoutes
{
    internal static readonly DeepWrit[][] Outer=[
        [
            new("The kitchen on the keel","One of Anja's pickling barrels has put out roots through a supply lighter. A broker calls the garden salvage. Anja calls it Thursday's lunch.","Distinguish the walking garden from the broker's decoys and escort the rooted lighter home.","Captain Brine","Anja serves the broker a pickle. He concedes that Thursday's lunch is properly the business of the kitchen."),
            new("The ladder under the marriage hall","Gio's old wedding guests remember steps down to the cooling pools. The walking terrace has folded those passages on top of one another. A couple waiting to be married has been climbing the same flight since dawn.","Open a continuous stair through the folded terrace to the pools.","The Knotted Handrail","The couple comes out at the wrong church and likes the view so much that they stay."),
            new("The soup fleet walks out","Sol has taught the kitchen skiffs to follow a pot of warm soup. A shore-fast squadron has requisitioned the pot to call the growing islands into its pens.","Find the supper signal among the anchor boats and lead the kitchen fleet out.","The Stock Judge","Sol changes the supper signal every night. The first code word is More."),
            new("A hole in the sixth pool","Peri keeps finding tiny footprints around a puddle nobody remembers filling. The young roots are taking water through a spring on the underside of the island. The spring's iron cap is almost closed.","Descend the root galleries and open the spring to the youngest pool.","The Corkback Crab","A trail of prints leads away in the morning. The little pool has set off to join the bigger ones."),
            new("A garden without a landlord","A bank has sent ships to buy the sea under the terraces. Uma is delighted to know they believe the sea will stay there while the gardeners sign.","Break the chain of survey prizes and recover the growers' traveling deeds.","Captain Groundrent","The survey ships float away from the ground they thought they had purchased. The growers keep the seeds.")
        ],[
            new("The bottles in the street","One orchard drifts into a licensing flotilla overnight. Rim recognizes the family tumblers by the chip that fits a grandmother's lip. Six ships have the same green bottle on their bow.","Identify the orchard prizes and bring the living glass back to the divers.","The Stopper Pike","The first toast is drunk from a glass with a lopsided rim. Every person at the table knows which side to use."),
            new("The inside of a helmet","Urs has lost the moss that tells a diver when air is getting thin. The last healthy bed grows inside a row of old helmets buried under the bottle reef.","Find the breathing galleries and bring their growing beds back to the diving school.","The Copper Seal","Each diver plants a pinch inside a helmet. The youngest diver gives hers a name and apologizes in advance for the damp."),
            new("The high-water shipment","Essa's siphon drew a crate higher than the harbor office believed water could rise. It is being carried away as evidence of an irregular tide. The crate has three reef calves breathing inside it.","Locate the sealed breathing crates and return their passengers to the orchard.","Captain Meniscus","The three calves blow bubbles all the way through the official hearing. The clerk writes Irregular in a very pleased hand."),
            new("The green floor","Van and Son ground the sharp edges off every bit of glass they ever sold. Down in the cullet stores a broken harvest has started growing sharp-side up.","Open a safe path through the buried cullet rooms for the divers' next planting.","The Bottle Mender","The new orchard floor is smooth enough to cross barefoot. Van goes across with his son to make sure."),
            new("The breathing vault","An old storage chamber holds the last bubble of air from the orchard before the migration. Cella knows two calves are sheltering in there. The glass is beginning to sing.","Reach the breathing vault and open a route for its calves into fresh water.","The Glassblower’s Lung","The bubble breaks in a soft rush of warm leaf smell. Every glass diver in the harbor takes one breath of their old garden.")
        ],[
            new("The lost second-place ribbon","Yali has spotted a prize ship flying a child's finish ribbon as a pennant. It belongs to a pilot who landed early to help a stranger. Half the fleet claims to have been that stranger.","Trace the starting marks on the courier sails and recover the right ribbon.","Commodore First","The pilot ties the ribbon to the ambulance wing. It comes home last nearly every day, with a passenger."),
            new("Below the sorting bells","Min's couriers sort letters by ringing different pitches. One bell keeps giving the note for urgent mail long after the exchange doors close.","Go down through the bell wells and find the forgotten urgent sack.","The Bellmouth Owl","The oldest letter is urgent only because somebody wanted an answer before supper. The family has the supper again and answers it."),
            new("A deed of feathers","Tem finds a feather pin in the rigging of a customs escort. Her fleet has been buying fallen pins to claim ownership of anyone who wears the matching wing.","Board the pin buyers and free the couriers from the false deeds.","The Feather Broker","The pilots write their own names on the pins and wear them upside down. It takes the clerks two weeks to notice."),
            new("Which end of the thread","Ivi can follow a wax seal back to its maker by its thread. A thread in the lower post tunnels leads past every official door, right into the rooms where the letters were opened.","Find the private sorting chambers and restore the broken seals to their letters.","The Ravel Reader","The opened letters go home with a note saying exactly who opened them. One father writes back to thank the clerk for correcting his spelling."),
            new("The race that stopped","Kest remembers a family under a flying island. Three race officials saw them as well and kept sailing. Each has hidden a different piece of the photograph aboard a private ship.","Recover the photographs and open a clear lane for the family’s return.","Captain Photo Finish","The three pieces fit together. The picture shows Kest losing the race by just enough to save four people.")
        ],[
            new("A quilt of forced sales","Fen recognizes half her hospital's blankets flying on anchor survey boats. Each carries a patient's initials in one corner. The patients have learned to signal with the loose ends.","Identify the signaling boats and return the missing blankets to the beds.","The Bedroll Admiral","The patients deliberately sew one square upside down in the new quilt. It is their own household flag."),
            new("The market under a lip","Lo hears a fishmonger calling from the old markets beneath the sleeping shoal. When the island breathes in, the narrow galleries shut. Its inhabitants have learned to trade between breaths.","Work the market levels and release the lower stockrooms to the tide.","The Slow Exhale","Lo buys two fish from below. The fishmonger gives one back because the island has just begun waking and everyone ought to have breakfast."),
            new("Pillows by the ton","Roe has found his quarry slate on a chain ship. The buyers plan to weigh down the sleeping shoal with the very stone it has been using for a pillow.","Take the quarry vessels and set the sleeping stones back on the warm side.","Captain Counterpoise","The shoal rolls its head to the new pillow. Half the neighboring market changes addresses without spilling one cup."),
            new("The clock in its jaw","Tab's clock keeps time with a sleeping island's teeth. A grain of anchor sand inside the lower wheel risks waking it with a sharp pain.","Descend the jaw galleries and release the clock without hurting the waking animal.","The Enamel Warden","Tab hears a yawn wide enough to empty a bay. The clock is late and the island is quite comfortable."),
            new("Who asked to be moved","Latt has the patients' consent forms. The infirmary lift has been locked by a tender that mistakes the forms for permission to move the island itself.","Open the lower infirmary routes and bring the patients to the beds they chose.","The Bedframe Bailiff","A lady who signed with a cross changes her mind halfway up the lift. Latt stops it and asks where she wants to go.")
        ],[
            new("House number thirteen","A salvage fleet is carrying the doors from Limpet Lane to a collector who has never been inside a house with a leak. Bo knows his door by the smell of the rain inside its wood.","Track the salvage fleet and bring the old doors alongside their households.","The Brass Visitor","Bo invites the collector in to see a real leak. They spend the rest of the evening fixing the gutter."),
            new("The watchmaker's cellar","A tin of Tuesday has sprung a leak through the ceiling of the old clock rooms. Rill has seen people coming out of the same door twice with different expressions.","Close the leaking hour and bring the service crew out of the clock cellars.","The Second Tuesday","The clock workers elect to keep their smiles from the second trip. Rill lets them take both lunch breaks."),
            new("The suit with two owners","A salvage insurer has seized a diving suit until its wearer can prove he is the only living thing inside it. Vim has counted one man, three little fish and a very shy shrimp.","Find the suit among the insurer’s dive tenders and return every occupant.","Captain Seam","Vim makes a label with a small space after the diver's name. Any new tenant can add a mark there."),
            new("The hot tap at midnight","Min's old bath attendants still make their rounds in the drowned rooms. A pipe that should run warm has begun sending up very cold bubbles at exactly midnight.","Trace the old hot-water line through the bath levels and bring the attendants home.","The Midnight Boiler","Min puts a towel on every hook. The next shift can find its way through by the smell of clean cotton."),
            new("The dinner bell sale","A private bell fleet is bidding on the drowned city's dinner bell by the weight of its bronze. Islet has a different measure. She can name the households that answered it.","Intercept the bell tenders and return the dinner signal to the listening fleet.","Captain Deadweight","The families thank the salvage hands first. Without anybody having to explain, the bell is given a place above the common table.")
        ],[
            new("The hoops at auction","Em recognizes every hoop on the governor's parade ships. A booming note belongs to a nursery drum, a dull one to a funeral boat. Neither belongs in a parade.","Identify the hoop ships by their notes and return the rings to the right households.","The Drum Major","A drum is allowed to sound nothing at all for the journey back. Em calls it the most respectful playing she has heard all week."),
            new("The quiet underneath","Dov keeps silence in a room under the drum floor. Something behind the quiet room has been swallowing the beat meant for the young islands.","Open the still chambers and carry the missing beat to the surface.","The Rest Keeper","The young islands answer after a long pause. Dov waits for the very smallest one before touching the sticks."),
            new("One heel in each boat","Sai made a pair of listening boots. A buyer split them between two patrol ships hoping to hear both sides of every conversation. Each pilot can hear only the other pilot's breakfast.","Find the two listening ships and reunite the boots on the public quay.","Captain Hobnail","The boots go back on the cobbler's feet. He can hear a couple dancing a street away and gives them the beat."),
            new("The sky in the basement","Uri's observatory looks at stars reflected in a drumhead. An anchor drill has cracked the skin underneath the lens. The night sky is running out through the floors.","Work down through the observatory and relieve the torn lower skin.","The Hollow Star","The stars settle back in their places. Two of them are flecks of brass from Uri's patch, and everyone agrees to leave them."),
            new("Two sides of a drum","Vara's account and Oren's were copied onto opposite sides of a great drum. The old acoustic chambers underneath it only let the audience hear one side at a time.","Open the twin listening galleries and return the last drum to both tellers.","The Double Listener","Vara begins. Oren waits. The gap between their accounts carries all the way to the smallest island.")
        ],[
            new("Fuel for an absent street","Dedel knows which houses are missing from the city by the order in which the old rosin ships unload. Somebody has been signing for one more street than the fleet can remember.","Follow the supply marks and return the phantom street’s fuel to its survivors.","The Rosin Factor","The people of the missing street warm their hands round a shared stove. Dedel has their names added to every future delivery."),
            new("The room where Sunday went","Agra remembers lunches on the breakwater. Its shelter chambers have gone dry while the bell ship carries the meals past. Toma has kept the key to the stair for years.","Open the breakwater shelters and find a passage to the floating Sunday table.","The Sunday Warden","The first lunch in the old shelter is a picnic. Nobody pretends the room is a whole city, and nobody eats alone."),
            new("The clerk's black pencil","Ivvy has found a ship's plan drawn solid black over the household berths. Six smaller craft have been sailing as ballast under those berths’ old names.","Mark the borrowed household names and free the ballast fleet.","Captain Graphite","The clerk sharpens a pencil and leaves the berths blank. The households fill their own names in over dinner."),
            new("How far a mast can bow","Mav's old mast hinge goes down through the memorial platform into chambers that were sealed when the city drowned. Toma once carried a small boy through those rooms on her back.","Open the lower hinge house and let the old mast bow to every family.","The Knee of Iron","The mast bows once toward open water. Toma takes a turn at the handle and passes it on before anyone can thank her."),
            new("The chain of kindness","Toma's anchor captains believe the nursery must be held still for its own safety. Most of them learned kindness during the flood. They will listen to a rescuer who boards their ship before she fires.","Find the rescue captains and bring their ships to the moving nursery.","The Last Fixed Point","One by one the captains let their anchors go. The oldest has tied a child's mitten to the shank so he will recognize it if he comes back.")
        ],[
            new("A field crossed out","The warm turnip beds have been entered in the buyers’ books as found land. Wem's very young gardeners have eaten all the boundary labels. The buyers are bringing some new ones.","Find the boundary fleet and leave the floating gardens open for breakfast.","The Furrow Broker","Wem plants the blank sides of the signs in the field. They hold up the peas quite well."),
            new("The room for very small things","Nix has recorded a newborn smaller than a thimble. It slipped down a measurement drain into rooms made to weigh the oldest islands. Every hatch is far too heavy for a young reef to open.","Work the lower scales and free the smallest calf from the weighing chambers.","The Big Measure","Nix makes a new entry less than one thumb wide. The little reef has grown by the time she finishes writing its name."),
            new("The hospital on wings","Reet's pelicans have taken sick calves aboard the wrong tender. A private nursery fleet feeds its patients only if it can keep the island after the patient grows up.","Identify the foster birds and return their calves to the visiting fleet.","Captain Down","A pelican drops a wet visiting card on Reet's boot. It is the first thank-you note the hospital has received from a bird."),
            new("A gate in the seabed","Ol's blue hinge has a twin below the bottom stair. The old gate down there was built to make sure the nursery never left the basin. A handprint on its plank is small enough to worry him.","Open the drowned gate chambers and give the youngest calves a way into the current.","The Closed Palm","The handprint came from a child pushing the gate open from the other side. Ol fits the plank above water where the next children can touch it."),
            new("Under the first footprint","Below the ring lie the footprints of islands that migrated before anyone lived on them. Between two prints Pip finds a small warm space left for a reef that has not yet been born.","Open the deep nursery passage and return with the route that belongs to the next herd.","The Sleeping Keel","Nell copies the empty space at the center of the page. There is no label. The child who comes after Pip can decide what belongs there.")
        ]
    ];
}
